ys and objects in terms of storing and accessing data, according to this lesson?#{1}":[168,176],"###Q10: Based on that difference, when should I choose to use an array, and when should I use an object?":[177,187],"###Q10: Based on that difference, when should I choose to use an array, and when should I use an object?#{1}":[179,187],"###Q11: The curly braces `{}` are used to define objects. I've also seen them used for code blocks in `if` statements or function bodies. Is this usage different?":[188,195],"###Q11: The curly braces `{}` are used to define objects. I've also seen them used for code blocks in `if` statements or function bodies. Is this usage different?#{1}":[190,195],"###Q12: The lesson mentions that objects are \"probably the most fundamental concept in the whole of JavaScript language.\" Why are they so important?":[196,203],"###Q12: The lesson mentions that objects are \"probably the most fundamental concept in the whole of JavaScript language.\" Why are they so important?#{1}":[198,203],"###Q13: How do I actually get the data _out_ of an object once I've created it (e.g., how do I get Jonas's first name from the `jonas` object)?":[204,208],"###Q13: How do I actually get the data _out_ of an object once I've created it (e.g., how do I get Jonas's first name from the `jonas` object)?#{1}":[206,208]},"outlinks":[],"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[19,27],[53,71],[86,93],[113,121],[133,143],[155,162]]},